{"name":"Pedestrian Lemon","hex":"#f7f72d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pedestrian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or intended for those who are walking.","Ordinary, dull; everyday; unexceptional."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A walker; one who walks or goes on foot, especially as opposed to one who uses a vehicle.","An expert or professional walker or runner; one who performs feats of walking or running."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pedestrian"},{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pedestrian","blocks":[{"text":"A pedestrian is a person traveling on foot, by wheelchair or with other mobility aids. Streets and roads often have a designated footpath for pedestrian traffic, called the sidewalk in North American English, the pavement in British English, and the footpath in Australian, Indian and New Zealand English. There are also footpaths not associated with thoroughfares; these include rural paths and urban short cuts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/CrossWalk_%285465840138%29.jpg/330px-CrossWalk_%285465840138%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pedestrian","wikidata":"Q221488"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/500px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/1280px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Pedestre.JPG/500px-Pedestre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sign in Belo Horizonte, Brazil, directing pedestrians to an overpass for safe crossing.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedestre.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG/500px-Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG/1280px-Colecci%C3%B3n_de_hombres_cruzando.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Colecc